## The brain-hygiene rule (read before writing any fact)

This is the part that makes the OS trustworthy. Three laws:

1. **One source of truth per fact.** Every fact has ONE canonical home (one official file that owns it) — see `SOURCES_OF_TRUTH.md` for the map and the precedence ladder (signed doc > customer/first-party > CRM > positioning). Derived views (`OKRS.md`, `CONTROL_CENTRE.md`) restate, never own.

2. **A gate on what gets in.** Every new input passes `INGESTION_GATE.md` (fact / validate / disregard) before it enters. **Numbers said to investors, customers, partners, or your audience are positioning, not fact. A flattering number is guilty until validated.** Stamp every fact with its source and date (its *provenance*).

3. **Human on the doubts.** On any clash — two files disagree, a number can't be stood up — surface both sides and ask me. **Never silently pick a winner.**

